  "notes": [
    "Ford (Thunderbird) drivers swept the top four finishing positions after sweeping the front row in pole qualifying. Ford would go on to win the Manufacturers' championship in 1992.",
    "Front row starters Sterling Marlin and Bill Elliott were involved in an accident on lap 92, ending both drivers' chances to win the race.",
    "Many other drivers sustained damage in the lap 92 accident, widely believed to be caused by Ernie Irvan: Irvan, Alan Kulwicki, Dale Earnhardt, Mark Martin, Darrell Waltrip, and others. Kulwicki finished forth with minimal damage.",
    "Michael Waltip, at this point winless in his Winstom Cup career, had a mechanical issue late while running in the lead pack in second position."
